THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
================================================================================

The projects below shaped fjader's design, and parts of its code are adapted
from Mosaic. Their licenses follow in full.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mosaic, by the UW Interactive Data Lab
https://github.com/uwdata/mosaic
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

fjader began as a Mosaic client, with @uwdata/mosaic-core as a dependency, and
its query layer is built on what Mosaic showed works. It replaced mosaic-core
with its own query layer when rendering in WebGPU required queries, GPU buffers
and Svelte's reactivity to be coupled more tightly than a general coordinator
provides. It still builds every query with @uwdata/mosaic-sql, a direct
dependency, and it kept Mosaic's ideas and, in places, the structure of
Mosaic's code:

- Pre-aggregation with sufficient statistics. The preaggregation code in
  src/lib/query-engine/ (sufficient-statistics.ts and preagg/) follows
  mosaic-core's preagg module: aggregates rewritten into partial statistics,
  FILTER clauses carried onto them, and preaggregated tables named by a hash
  of their query.
- The crossfilter selection model, in which a selection clause filters every
  mark except those its source excludes.
- The REST connector protocol, which the Python query server speaks.
- vgplot's API style, its interactors (interval brushes, toggles) and its
  JSON spec layout (hconcat, vconcat), without being compatible with vgplot.

Mosaic's license, reproduced in full, including its own notice for the parts
it derives from Observable Plot:

